+# 🌉 Bridge Work Order — [P2] Memory graph store empty (graph_nodes: 0) despite 20-tool memory layer running (bridge-20261027-memory-graph-empty)
+
+## Problem
+Verified live 2026-10-25:
+
+- `memory_status` → `ready: true, toolCount: 20, lastError: null`
+- `memory_get_session_stats` → `{"session_id":"default","active_episodes":12,"graph_nodes":0}`
+- `memory_read_graph` / `memory_search_nodes` therefore operate on an empty graph — entity/relation memory is structurally present and structurally unused
+- Every guest client in `agent_status` runs on `tenant_default` with `session_id: default` — no per-user memory namespace is being exercised either
+
+The studio ships onboarding (`OnboardingWizard`, `StepFirstChat`) but conversations leave no persistent, searchable user memory — the exact capability (AIQ-057/098/099) that makes Monica feel personal across sessions.
+
+## Impact (AIQ mapping)
+- AIQ-057 🟡 memory used only within episodes; no entity graph, no cross-session recall surface
+- AIQ-098 🟡 expiry/TTL policy undocumented; delete tools exist but nothing to delete
+- AIQ-099 🟡 session vs long-term separation untested with real data
+
+## Fix (smallest safe change)
+1. Wire chat pipeline writes: after each completed session, upsert entities/relations via existing `memory_create_entities`/`memory_add_observations` (namespaced `tenant:user:session`)
+2. Add TTL + recency policy to episode store (config knob in env.ts, fail-loud pattern)
+3. Studio surface: "remembered context" chips in workspace UI showing what memory informed the answer, with a per-item forget button (satisfies AIQ-062 transparency)
+4. Seed test: two-session script where session 2 correctly recalls session 1 facts
+
+## Acceptance Criteria
+- [ ] `graph_nodes > 0` after a real chat session
+- [ ] Cross-session recall verified by scripted 2-session test
+- [ ] Forget button removes the entity end-to-end
+- [ ] No cross-tenant memory bleed (query with foreign tenantId returns empty)
+
+## Reflection Evidence (why + alternatives_rejected)
+**Why:** memory is the highest-retention feature in consumer AI; the infra is already paid for and idle.
+**Alternatives rejected:** (a) new vector store — Qdrant + memory tools already deployed; (b) client-side memory — defeats tenant isolation goals.
+
+## Labels
+`bridge:queued` `P2-medium` `area:memory` `AIQ:057` `AIQ:098` `AIQ:099`
